  "reason": "Evidence: config_038 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + concat, multiprofile) is the current best at 0.7207 acc, and all multimodal results so far use concat fusion. We have no data on whether weighted fusion could improve or degrade performance relative to concat under the best-known representation settings. Question: config_039 is identical to config_038 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, isolating the fusion-strategy effect with a single-variable comparison. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly exploits the strongest evidence (best RNA encoder, best image encoder, multiprofile, transformer aggregation) while testing the one untested design axis at that operating point. A clear win or loss on fusion method will either yield an immediate performance gain or confirm concat suffices, freeing the next budget slot to probe aggregation or image-encoder contribution. This is more informative than, e.g., testing avgpool (already near-equivalent to transformer in RNA-only) or a weaker RNA encoder, both of which have lower expected information gain per experiment."
